[2026-08-29T15:25:28.745Z] [Telegram] → chat 8844466799: ▶️ Auto-resume finished after the key rotation.📋 5/8 tasks completed so far. |  | ## Summary |  | **Nothing pending is actionable** — all three remaining items are explicitly deferred/blocked. |  | ### Completed (already checked off) | - **P0:** #1 drag-hide scoping, #2 vertical scrolling | - **P1:** #3 playhead listener scoping, #4 timeline payload cache | - **P2:** #8 keyframe crystal visibility | - **Layout fixes:** interpolation pill height, key bar heights, lane label/`✕` overlap |  | ### Remaining (3 items — all blocked) |  | | # | Task | Blocker | | |---|------|---------| | | **5** | Batch keying/interpolation commands | Needs a new **batched command API on the editor controller / MCP side**. `_ensureEdgeKeys` fires up to 6 awaited commands per selected node, `_groupInterpolationControl` one per channel, and each triggers a full `notifyListeners()`. Can't fix from this package — requires upstream API design first. | | | **6** | `previewDuration` decodes all channel timelines every tick | Root cause lives in `editor_controller.dart:751` (`_onTick` non-loop end check). Fix belongs in the controller, so it's deferred together with #5 — same upstream dependency. | | | **7** | Tighten `hitKey` row scoping (12px radius vs 22px rows) | **Documented as intentional upstream behavior** — the oversized hit radius is meant to make dense rigs feel forgiving (tapping near a key selects it rather than scrubbing). Changing the "feel" needs discussion before touching it. | |  | ### Recommendation | No further code changes can be made here without upstream coordination. If you want progress, the next step is opening a discussion with the `flutter_scene_editor_core` maintainers about the batched-command API (#5/#6) and confirming whether the hit-radius feel is still desired (#7).
